      "writtenOn": "2021-01-19T19:14:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe??? Currently bpf programs are just always root-owned AFAICR.\n\nBasides atm. these are accessed/attached from netd... which runs as root.\n\nMaybe this is something we should change after everything is running from the mainline module.\n\nBut note that the privs are read-for-all 0444 anyway, so the ownership doesn\u0027t matter much, besides potentially protecting against deletion [though selinux will protect against that too], so it would only provide benefit if we also reduced 0444 to 0440 or 0400.",
      "parentUuid": "4d6ca8b2_f9579906",
