      "writtenOn": "2021-01-20T02:14:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discussion: IIRC we added the uid and group parameters so these programs can be set to group ID net_admin:\n\n$ adb shell ls -l /sys/fs/bpf | grep net_admin\n-r--r----- 1 root net_admin     0 2021-01-20 10:31 prog_netd_skfilter_allowlist_xtbpf\n-r--r----- 1 root net_admin     0 2021-01-20 10:31 prog_netd_skfilter_denylist_xtbpf\n-r--r----- 1 root net_admin     0 2021-01-20 10:31 prog_netd_skfilter_egress_xtbpf\n-r--r----- 1 root net_admin     0 2021-01-20 10:31 prog_netd_skfilter_ingress_xtbpf\n\nThe reason was that vendor code in the net_admin group could change iptables rules, which requires reading the program.\n\nSo I think this should probably be AID_ROOT, AID_NETWORK_STACK with a TODO to change it to AID_NETWORKSTACK, AID_NETWORKSTACK if/when we move the attach to the networkstack module.",
